{
  "_comment": "Commentary (Tasks 123-124; docs/channel.md §18.2): short calls at key moments of live matches and re-airs, never highlights. One commentator per match (never two in one match): the semifinals and the final always playoffs (the Announcer, Tom); the final round's simultaneous matches each a different one; otherwise picked by the seed from the commentators onAir. Each commentator's clips are made ahead of time by `npm run voices -- --assets` into assets/voices/<id>/<line id>.wav: engine kokoro (voice = Kokoro's voice id) or elevenlabs (voice = ElevenLabs' voice id; v3, excited lines tagged [excited]; only made with --paid, during a paid month, vision §12); speed = how quickly it speaks (1 is the voice's own pace). A commentator goes onAir once its clips are made and approved. lines: text as written, say as spoken (an exclamation mark makes the call excited; a full stop calmer). moments: the lines each moment can call (kickoff, second_half, half_time, full_time and their _level forms come after the whistle; passing after settings.commentary.passRun passes in a row, holding when one outfield player keeps it settings.commentary.holdSeconds (both counted as the picture draws them; Task 149 added tackle and steal, each mixed with the either lines, holding, foul, and the Announcer's playoff moments full_time_semi, full_time_final, golden_goal and overtime). A line with voices is made and spoken only by those commentators. A line with warm true (a holding line, That ball's getting warm) is said only once the heat meter is Warm or Hot (Tom, 2026-10-18). rate: the share of a moment called at all (the frequent ones; 1 if left out), chance: the share called within minGapSeconds of another moment. A moment with onAir false isn't called (its clips not made yet); golden_goal then falls back to goal or scorcher, the playoffs' full times to full_time. Task 150 made the new moments' clips and put them on air by one team, counted as the picture draws them), dealt in a seeded shuffle so none repeats until the rest have had a turn, and the chance it's called when it comes within minGapSeconds of another moment (a moment on its own is always called; goals always win). Timing (delay, gap, ducking) is in config/settings.json → commentary.",
